WEBVTT

00:04.650 --> 00:06.912
This is Allen Company task training for loader

00:06.912 --> 00:10.200
operators. Loaders do more jobs at a quarry than

00:10.200 --> 00:12.912
any other machine: loading trucks, feeding the

00:12.912 --> 00:15.737
plant, building and working stockpiles,

00:15.737 --> 00:18.938
cleaning up spills. That variety is exactly what

00:18.938 --> 00:20.375
makes them dangerous.

00:21.492 --> 00:23.992
A wheel loader steers by bending in the middle.

00:23.992 --> 00:26.654
When it turns, the gap between the front and rear

00:26.654 --> 00:29.755
frames closes completely. Never stand in that pinch

00:29.755 --> 00:32.542
zone while the engine is running. Before anyone

00:32.542 --> 00:35.142
works near the hinge, install the steering frame

00:35.142 --> 00:37.804
lock, the bar built for that, and shut the machine

00:37.804 --> 00:38.517
down.

00:39.630 --> 00:42.605
Examine the loader before use every shift.

00:42.605 --> 00:45.330
Tires and rims, hoses and cylinders,

00:45.330 --> 00:48.480
the bucket and its pins, lights, horn,

00:48.480 --> 00:52.005
backup alarm, cameras and mirrors, the ROPS and

00:52.005 --> 00:55.117
the seat belt, the extinguisher and the steps.

00:55.117 --> 00:58.068
Defects that affect safety: tag it out and report

00:58.068 --> 01:00.893
it. Record the inspection. Buckle up before it

01:00.893 --> 01:01.742
moves.

01:05.068 --> 01:07.481
The bucket and lift arms block your view to the

01:07.481 --> 01:10.281
front, and the engine hood blocks the rear.

01:10.281 --> 01:12.631
Anyone approaching a loader makes contact with

01:12.631 --> 01:15.243
the operator and gets an answer back before they

01:15.243 --> 01:18.606
come closer. As the operator, warn before you start

01:18.606 --> 01:21.056
or move, and stop if you lose track of someone

01:21.056 --> 01:22.143
near your machine.

01:23.266 --> 01:25.703
Travel with the bucket low, just high enough to

01:25.703 --> 01:28.741
clear the ground. A raised, loaded bucket moves

01:28.741 --> 01:31.078
the center of gravity up and forward,

01:31.078 --> 01:33.666
and that's how loaders roll over, especially on

01:33.666 --> 01:36.741
slopes and turns. Go up and down grades with the

01:36.741 --> 01:38.329
load pointed uphill.

01:39.472 --> 01:41.660
When you park or leave the machine,

01:41.660 --> 01:44.035
lower the bucket to the ground, set the parking

01:44.035 --> 01:47.035
brake, and on a grade, chock it or turn it into

01:47.035 --> 01:47.922
a bank.

01:51.254 --> 01:53.329
When you load a truck, the driver stays in the

01:53.329 --> 01:56.566
cab. That's an Allen rule. Never swing a loaded

01:56.566 --> 01:59.742
bucket over the cab. Load evenly; an off-center

01:59.742 --> 02:02.629
load can tip a truck on a ramp. Watch for rocks

02:02.629 --> 02:04.604
that hang over the edge of the body.

02:05.720 --> 02:07.695
Load to the target weight you're given.

02:07.695 --> 02:10.520
An overloaded truck has less braking on haul roads

02:10.520 --> 02:13.308
and ramps, and puts the driver at risk.

02:16.626 --> 02:20.663
At a stockpile, never undercut the face so it overhangs.

02:20.663 --> 02:23.863
Material can let go all at once and bury a loader.

02:23.863 --> 02:26.676
Keep the face no higher than your machine can reach,

02:26.676 --> 02:29.413
work it from the side, and never let anyone walk

02:29.413 --> 02:31.851
at the toe of a pile. There's a full lesson on

02:31.851 --> 02:34.576
stockpiles in the Allen video library.

02:35.700 --> 02:38.475
At the face, nobody works or travels between the

02:38.475 --> 02:41.062
loader and the highwall or bank where they could

02:41.062 --> 02:44.000
be caught. And as Allen rule: never work near a

02:44.000 --> 02:45.762
highwall with your back to it.

02:46.878 --> 02:50.028
At a hopper, use the bumper block. Never drive

02:50.028 --> 02:52.928
or walk out onto a surge pile or bin that's being

02:52.928 --> 02:55.828
drawn from underneath. A hidden void can collapse

02:55.828 --> 02:56.628
under you.

02:59.944 --> 03:02.944
Never work under a raised bucket or arms held only

03:02.944 --> 03:06.406
by hydraulics. Lower it, or block it securely with

03:06.406 --> 03:08.956
the cylinder lock or cribbing. Then lock out the

03:08.956 --> 03:09.781
machine.

03:10.906 --> 03:13.506
Nobody rides or is lifted in the bucket,

03:13.506 --> 03:16.243
ever. And look up for power lines before you raise

03:16.243 --> 03:17.418
the bucket near them.

03:20.732 --> 03:24.607
Recap: examine before use and tag safety defects.

03:24.607 --> 03:27.844
Belt on. Nobody in the pinch zone. Make contact

03:27.844 --> 03:31.007
and get an answer back. Bucket low when you travel,

03:31.007 --> 03:34.244
down when you park. No overhanging faces,

03:34.244 --> 03:36.707
nobody between the machine and the wall,

03:36.707 --> 03:40.032
nobody on surge piles. Block raised parts.

03:40.032 --> 03:41.807
Nobody rides in the bucket.

03:42.926 --> 03:46.088
Remember: your site's plans and procedures always

03:46.088 --> 03:47.588
override this video.
